#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134596} :activity/id #uuid "682c47c0-744b-5245-9512-733920b3dc7e" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050838 :topic/id #uuid "6a8e722d-b3fa-5144-a35c-61c8756571f7" :topic/math-academy-id 2195} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134596 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186135183 :tutorial/content "To **cube** a number means to multiply that number by itself and then multiply the result by the original number once more.\n\nFor example, to \"cube $2$\", we need to multiply $2$ by $2$ to make $4,$ and then multiply this result by $2$ once more. We write the \"cube of $2$\" as $2^3,$ so we have\n\n$$\n2^3 = \\underbrace{2\\cdot 2}_{\\large 4} \\cdot 2 = 4 \\cdot 2 = 8.\n$$\n\nWe would then say that \"the cube of $2$ is $8$\". We could also say \"$2$ cubed equals $8$\".\n\nThe number ${\\color{blue}3}$ in the expression $2^{\\color{blue}3}$ is called the power (or exponent).\n\nThe act of cubing a number can be represented geometrically. For example, let's start by representing the number $2$ with the following collection of two items:\n\n![](images/b6/b6a13017dcbcf25a66ab576189690e8879a4ccbb3c4c5562b129f4dd15af4e85.png)\n\nThen we can picture $2^3$ by creating a bigger shape (called a **cube**) with length, width and height all equal to $2\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/30/305e02bdaa4c3efcb9d8047eeb3d3573f39c08714e30ba6053cfc4441053156b.png)\n\nThere are $8$ items in total in our big cube (one little cube is hiding behind the others), indicating that $2^3=8.$\n\nClearly, $1^3=1\\cdot1\\cdot1={\\color{blue}1}.$ The next few first basic cubes are shown below:\n\n| $2^3=2 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 2={\\color{blue}8}$ | $3^3=3 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 3={\\color{blue}27}$ | $4^3=4 \\cdot 4 \\cdot 4={\\color{blue}64}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ![](images/30/305e02bdaa4c3efcb9d8047eeb3d3573f39c08714e30ba6053cfc4441053156b.png) | ![](images/cb/cb3171dc7f7a2e9838c3e8b46c3ce385be28624b4474391b9bb211b5a599fa55.png) | ![](images/65/6546ffc5df407b29df601252e1f5afa8e01b17dca5c7169a6321d550d86255c3.png) |\n\nThe cubes of our usual counting numbers are called **cube numbers** or **perfect cubes**. We can write them as follows:\n\n$$\n1^3, 2^3, 3^3, 4^3, 5^3, 6^3, \\ldots \\qquad \\text{or} \\qquad {\\color{blue}1}, {\\color{blue}8}, {\\color{blue}27}, {\\color{blue}64}, {\\color{blue}125}, {\\color{blue}216}, \\ldots\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "1bd95aec-179b-5dc4-b7bd-da02ca5932f2" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8272 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "9ccabb01-ff56-5686-b294-bd66b4e89e88" :step/math-academy-id 151851 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134597}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134597 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133738 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133511 :question/id #uuid "3e2f3025-cfc0-5688-a5be-dbe7f98848e3" :question/math-academy-id "e-13248"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "39ed44f2-c5ca-5920-9bb0-4ea26ff3207a" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050428}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134411} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134570} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475924} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475985}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cube of a Number"} :step/id #uuid "45f96aa2-301d-5486-9223-105546674dc7" :step/math-academy-id 151852 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134598}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134598 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186135184 :tutorial/content "Cubing a negative number *always* results in another negative number.\n\nThis is because a negative times a negative gives a positive value, and then a positive times a negative is a negative again:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-)\\,\\cdot \\,(-)\\,\\cdot \\,(-)\\,=\\,{{(-)\\,\\cdot \\,(-)}_{⏟}}_{(+)}\\,\\cdot \\,(-)\\,=\\,(+)\\,\\cdot \\,(-)\\,=\\,(-)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor example,\n\n$$\n({\\color{red}-5})^3 = \\underbrace{({\\color{red}-5}) \\cdot ({\\color{red}-5})}_{\\large {\\color{blue}25}} \\cdot ({\\color{red}-5}) = {\\color{blue}25} \\cdot ({\\color{red}-5}) = {\\color{red}-125}.\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "e462ead2-4e55-5dac-a940-22768a77546e" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8273 :tutorial/title "The Cube of a Negative Number"} :step/id #uuid "fd815b69-da3f-5d4e-b49a-e75f1d8f0398" :step/math-academy-id 151856 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134599}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134599 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133739 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133512 :question/id #uuid "02fa99aa-811e-5d0a-b278-24ec7697a038" :question/math-academy-id "e-13249"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4cb81a65-ae88-591a-bb87-0ecb7124b154" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049349} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050287}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134346} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134412} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475917} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475936} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475957} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475977}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cube of a Negative Number"} :step/id #uuid "79b94128-fada-50aa-8ec5-3f3315b85c77" :step/math-academy-id 151857 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134600}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134600 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133740 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133513 :question/id #uuid "5468caae-f88a-59d2-98ab-7941bf7cd81a" :question/math-academy-id "e-13251"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "70e7585e-7380-5dbc-9272-b358f085429c" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049253}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134347} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134383} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424819} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475961} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475972}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cube of a Fraction"} :step/id #uuid "266a9ffe-5ee6-5f21-95a7-a8aea3b7a60d" :step/math-academy-id 151861 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134601}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134601 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133741 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133514 :question/id #uuid "ba7b4d05-42b6-58a5-9607-b30742991005" :question/math-academy-id "e-13253"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "09de45b3-1a35-55e3-9886-2e0533f237d6" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049194}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134151} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134510} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475958} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475968}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cube of a Decimal"} :step/id #uuid "2fd6a3e8-b2b4-5760-a3c1-067f79a80a5b" :step/math-academy-id 151864}] :activity/title "Cubing Rational Numbers" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186134039}]}
